author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "A declared identity vocabulary exists as versioned workspace data that maps every literal author spelling observed in the record to a canonical harness, and the map is data rather than code so a workspace can extend it for its own historical spellings; Every grouping and filtering surface resolves author through the alias map, so a query for one harness returns the union of its spellings, proven against the live corpus where claude-code-agent and harness:claude-code must group together and codex-agent, harness:codex and codex-root must group together; History is never rewritten to normalize identity: a test asserts that applying the alias map changes no stored entry and no hash, and that verification still passes byte for byte afterwards; The alias map is itself versioned and recorded, so a reader can reproduce how a given spelling was interpreted at a given time rather than only how it is interpreted now; A newly asserted author is either validated against the declared domain or recorded with a marker that separates it from a detected identity, and the existing author_source values gain an enforcement path rather than remaining descriptive; A coverage report states how many entries resolve to a canonical harness, how many remain unresolved, and which unresolved spellings are most frequent, so the residual is measurable rather than estimated; The documentation states that a detected identity is an unverified claim and that the alias map is an interpretation layer, never evidence of who actually ran a command"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: high
confidence: 85
resolution: Added a versioned workspace-extensible legacy author vocabulary interpreted at read time with bounded residual reporting.
expected_result: "Historical spellings resolve reproducibly to canonical harnesses without rewriting immutable entries or hashes, while unresolved vocabulary remains measurable."
actual_result: "Merged PR #874 preserves stored authors and hashes, exposes vocabulary version and canonical harness projections, supports workspace aliases, reports bounded unresolved spellings, and passes full gates plus isolated consumer acceptance."
